## Can You Claim Musk's SpaceX Share Yet?

No, there is nothing to claim or sign up for anywhere today. As of October 19, 2026, neither Elon Musk nor [SpaceX](https://www.spacex.com/) has launched an application, reservation form, or official portal for the pledged shares. Musk posted on X that he plans to give one share to every child in America next year, but nothing official has been published beyond that social post. No agency, company, or broker has opened a registration list.

What to do now:
1. Nothing for the share itself: no form, account, or app step reserves it today.
2. Watch for official terms from Musk or SpaceX that name how the shares would be delivered.
3. Ignore any message offering to claim, reserve, or speed up the share.

Our guidance would change if Musk or SpaceX publishes official terms that name a delivery route. Until an official framework appears, no action can secure a promised share.

This waiting posture is not for families who want their children invested immediately. If you want your child to own SpaceX stock now, buy it in a custodial account opened by an adult. Review our guide on [how to buy SpaceX stock](/guides/how-to-buy-spacex-stock/) to see how custodial trading works on [Nasdaq](https://www.nasdaq.com/).